<title>POLAND: POLISH CENTRAL BANK SELLS PLN 273 MLN NBP-BILLS.</title>
<headline>POLISH CENTRAL BANK SELLS PLN 273 MLN NBP-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland sold 122 million zlotys of its 91-day NBP-bills and 150 million zlotys of 182-day NBP-bills, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The bank sold the shorter paper at an unchanged average yield of 22.00 percent.</p>
<p>The average yield of the longer paper rose 0.01 point to 21.99 percent from the last auction on January 17, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
</text>
